1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,440
The numbers now required a room of their own, and the reality they described was worse than the practical one.

2
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:12,115
“The figure for the circle of payers is a square peg,” the editor wrote.

3
00:00:12,115 --> 00:00:23,884
“It does not fit at any angle.” The observer and the adviser had both signed the headline, and neither of them was willing to defend it in public.

4
00:00:23,884 --> 00:00:29,943
The ban on new connections was a severe violation of the fabric of the old town.

5
00:00:29,943 --> 00:00:36,868
“A defensive policy with an offensive punishment is not morality,” the adviser said.

6
00:00:36,868 --> 00:00:49,207
“It is a denial dressed as a bargain.” A harsh winter, a reluctant council, and a loyalty to the old tariff had produced the whole crisis.

7
00:00:49,207 --> 00:00:55,676
The insert in the periodical was an invitation to the public to publicize its own bills.

8
00:00:55,676 --> 00:00:59,746
“Fame is not the point,” the editor said.

9
00:00:59,746 --> 00:01:12,655
“A household that is penalized for using water is a fact, not a headline.” The consultative committee met in a church hall and played chess afterwards.

10
00:01:12,655 --> 00:01:21,259
The cruelty of the numbers was their symmetry: the circle of payers and the circle of users were drawn in the same square.

11
00:01:21,259 --> 00:01:26,509
“A cruel inference is still an inference,” the adviser said.

12
00:01:26,509 --> 00:01:31,798
“You can forbid the word and you cannot forbid the arithmetic.”

13
00:01:31,798 --> 00:01:34,613
The betrayal was in the timing.

14
00:01:34,613 --> 00:01:40,388
“We were told to oversee a process and not a war,” the observer wrote.

15
00:01:40,388 --> 00:01:52,867
“The warfare of two departments has produced a diplomacy of delays.” The editor's denial of the first draft was, in the end, correct.

16
00:01:52,867 --> 00:02:00,226
The real issue came into the room at last: who draws the circle, and with what instrument.

17
00:02:00,226 --> 00:02:10,875
The air in the hall was cold, the water in the well was low, and the group had, for the first time, a long list and a short time.

18
00:02:10,875 --> 00:02:20,359
The order of the day was not an act of hell but a development we had to get through; the inviting insert in the periodical told us so.

19
00:02:20,359 --> 00:02:31,844
The room, the square, and the air in it were all part of the same period, and the editor asked us to defend the headline once more.
